# .dockerignore — repo-root build-context filter (whitelist).
#
# SERVES TWO CONSUMERS (both build with the repo/worktree ROOT as the
# docker context):
#
#   1. docker/selftest/Dockerfile (native-engine self-test battery):
#      needs go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, internal/, docker/selftest/ ONLY —
#      the point is a TINY context (this slice's requirement).
#   2. The two auto-classifier-pilot compose images
#      (tests/integration/auto-gate-live-http/docker-compose.yml and
#      tests/e2e/auto-gate-classifier/docker-compose.yml, both with
#      context: ../../..):
#        - Dockerfile.tester: templates/overlays/auto-classifier-pilot/
#          plugins, templates/sys-prompts/, the integration test.mjs;
#        - Dockerfile.e2e-runner: `COPY . .` + go build of the
#          vh-agent-harness binary (corpus.go, core_manifest.go,
#          templates/ for go:embed) + the e2e driver + profile.
#
# STYLE: default-deny (`*`) + explicit re-includes. This PRESERVES the
# previous file's leak-prevention guard with a stronger form: refs/ (a
# local reference bundle with third-party product names that must NEVER
# enter an image layer), worktrees/, .git, docs/, researches/, tests/
# beyond the two subtrees, rendered state (.opencode/), overlay state
# (.vh-agent-harness/, .local/) — none are re-included, so none can
# ship. The mock-llm services build with their own directory as the
# context, so this root file does not affect them.
*
# --- selftest battery (docker/selftest/Dockerfile) ---
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!cmd/**
!internal
!internal/**
!docker
!docker/selftest
!docker/selftest/**
# --- pre-existing root-context consumers (compose images above) ---
!corpus.go
!core_manifest.go
!templates
!templates/**
# tests/: only the two subtrees the root-context Dockerfiles COPY;
# everything else under tests/ stays excluded.
!tests
tests/*
!tests/e2e
tests/e2e/*
!tests/e2e/auto-gate-classifier
!tests/e2e/auto-gate-classifier/**
!tests/integration
tests/integration/*
!tests/integration/auto-gate-live-http
!tests/integration/auto-gate-live-http/**
